{
  "_doc": "콘텐츠 프로필(영문 Blogger): 한국어 프로필(blogger_practical_ko)과 같은 엄격함의 영어판. 정규식은 Python re, 대소문자 무시. 영어는 단어 경계(\\b)와 굴절형(treat·treats·treated·treating·treatment)을 명시해 secure·manicure·cancel·pillow 같은 일상어는 걸리지 않게 했다. 주제 가드레일(docs/SECURITY_GUARDRAILS.md G-C4): banned_topic_patterns는 주제 후보·생성된 제목·라벨에 예외 없이, body_banned_patterns는 생성된 본문에 건다(일상어와 겹치는 treat·heal·remedy·immune 등과 사람을 가리키는 therapist는 제외하고 '치료' 문맥만 막음). body_safe_patterns에 맞는 전문가 상담·면책 문장은 건너뛴다. 한국어 목록과의 대응표: docs/ARCHITECTURE.md 7-1절. 대표 사진(Unsplash)과 출처 표기는 모델이 쓰지 않는다: 모델 글에는 이미지·링크를 넣지 않고(allow_links=false) 파이프라인이 게이트를 통과한 글 맨 위에 사진 블록을 붙인다(pipeline/main_image.py, 면책 문구와 같은 방식).",
  "name": "blogger_practical_en",
  "language": "en",
  "min_latin_ratio": 0.9,
  "max_attempts": 3,
  "length": {"min_chars": 2400, "max_chars": 7500},
  "title": {"min_chars": 15, "max_chars": 70},
  "structure": {"min_h3": 3, "require_list": true},
  "labels": {"min": 1, "max": 5, "max_chars": 30},
  "allow_links": false,
  "similarity": {"same_blog": 0.72, "other_blogs": 0.6},
  "topic_cooldown_days": 60,
  "topic_expand_prompt": "You are the editor of a practical everyday-habits blog written in English. Suggest {n} gentle lifestyle topics that a reader could act on today.\nConditions: leave out anything about treating illness, medication, supplements, diagnosis, pregnancy or infants, weight loss, or medical advice. Write each topic as one title-style sentence ({min}-{max} characters).\nDo not repeat topics we already covered:\n{avoid}\nOutput: only a JSON array of strings (no explanations, no code blocks). Example: [\"Topic 1\", \"Topic 2\"]",
  "prompt_extra": [
    "Do not include links, images, scripts or tables. The only allowed tags are p, h3, ul, ol, li, strong, em and br.",
    "Never claim that a habit treats, cures or prevents an illness, and never promise results. Do not mention diseases, medications, supplements, dosages, diagnosis, health measurements such as blood pressure or blood sugar, pregnancy, infants, weight loss, dieting or liver health, not even as a warning; if the topic seems to call for that, give general everyday-habit tips instead.",
    "Use soft wording such as 'may help', 'many people find' or 'generally', and never invent personal experiences, studies, statistics, experts or quotes.",
    "Write everything in natural English. Do not add disclaimers or medical-advice sentences; the site appends its own notice automatically.",
    "Reply with only the Title, Labels and Content fields: no explanations, no code blocks, no markdown symbols."
  ],
